<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Enmebaragesi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 2700 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/28th-century-bce">28th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Enmebaragesi was a king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kish">Kish</a> who lived around 2700 BCE and is one of the earliest Mesopotamian rulers attested in inscriptions. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sumerian-king-list">Sumerian King List</a> records that he defeated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elamites">Elamites</a>, among the earliest recorded conflicts in the history of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elamite-confederation">Elamite Confederation</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/enmebaragesi.jpg" alt="Enmebaragesi" width="320" height="298" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: पाटलिपुत्र · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mebaragsi,_King_of_Kish_(transcription_of_fragment,_original_in_Iraq_National_Museum).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
